hadiths[23]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1984","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lets his garment hang below the ankles (such as shalwar, trousers, pajama, etc.), he will burn in the Fire."""
"1985","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked ""Habrah"", that is, the Yemeni sheet (to wear), more than all other clothes."
"1986","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, he was covered in a ""Burdi Yamani"" (a Yemeni sheet)."
"1987","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him): I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sleeping, dressed in white clothes. Then after a short while, I came again and he was awake. At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says the statement 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah) and dies upon it, will certainly enter Paradise."" I asked, ""Even if he committed adultery and theft?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""Even if he committed adultery and theft."" I asked again, ""Even if he committed adultery and theft?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""Even if he committed adultery and theft."" I asked a third time, ""Even if he committed adultery and theft?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""Even if he committed adultery and theft. (And) may Abu Dharr's nose be rubbed in dust."" (Meaning, even if Abu Dharr dislikes it.) And whenever Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith, he would (proudly) say, ""May Abu Dharr's nose be rubbed in dust."""
"1988","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade silk clothing except to the extent—then the Prophet (peace be upon him) joined his index and middle fingers and showed (i.e., it is permissible up to the width of two fingers). By this, he meant the border or embroidery of the cloth."
"1989","It is narrated from Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever wears silk clothing in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."""
"1990","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us: ""Do not eat or drink in utensils of gold and silver, do not wear silk, harir, or dibaj, and do not sit on them (nor make them bedding)."""
"1991","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade men from wearing saffron-colored (clothes)."
"1992","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): He was asked whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while wearing shoes. He replied: ""Yes."" (The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while wearing shoes.)"
"1993","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should walk wearing a shoe on one foot only; rather, he should wear both shoes or take off both."""
"1994","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever among you puts on shoes should start with the right side, and when taking them off, should start with the left side, so that the right foot is the first to be put on and the last to be taken off."""
"1995","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a silver ring (according to the custom of that time for sealing, etc.) and had ""Muhammad Rasul Allah"" engraved on it, and said: ""I have taken a silver ring and had 'Muhammad Rasul Allah' engraved on it. It is not permissible for anyone to have a ring engraved in the same way."""
"1996","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed effeminate men and masculine women and said: ""Expel them from your houses."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) expelled such-and-such effeminate men, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) expelled such-and-such masculine women."
"1997","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Oppose the polytheists, let the beard grow, and trim the moustache."""
"1998","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Jews and Christians do not dye their hair, so you should do the opposite of them."" (That is, dye your hair. However, it is necessary to avoid black color.)"
"1999","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was neither curly nor very straight, but was in a moderate and balanced state, and it reached between his ears and shoulders."
"2000","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had flesh on his hands and feet, and his blessed face was extremely beautiful. I have never seen anyone as beautiful as him before or after him. The palms of his hands were broad and wide."
"2001","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding shaving part of the head and leaving part unshaven."
"2002","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I used to apply perfume, which was the best fragrance of that time, to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) with my own hand, and I would perceive the fragrance in his blessed head and beard."
"2003","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not refuse the gift of perfume."
"2004","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: In the year of the Farewell Hajj, at the time of entering into Ihram and at the time of exiting from Ihram, I applied the perfume of Dhareer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with my own hand."
"2005","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those who make pictures will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: 'Give life to what you have created.'"""
"2006","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say, ""Allah Almighty says: Who is more unjust than the one who wishes to create like Me? (If he is such a creator,) then let him create a grain of wheat or let him create an ant."" In another narration, it is added: ""Let him produce the grain (i.e., the produce) and show it."""
